   796	if [ -z "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-}" ] && [ -n "${SESSION_ENV_PATH:-}" ] && [ -f "$SESSION_ENV_PATH" ]; then
   797	  CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT=$(awk 'BEGIN{p="LARCH_CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT="} index($0,p)==1{print substr($0,length(p)+1); exit}' "$SESSION_ENV_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true)
   798	fi
   799	export CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT
   800	SESSION_ENV_PATH="$SESSION_ENV_PATH" LARCH_TIMING_SKILL=design "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/timing-ledger.sh" mark "design Step 5 — cleanup" || true
   801	```
   802	
   803	### 5a — Update Reviewer Presence Status
   804	
   805	### 5b — Final approval gate + write `larch:plan` to GitHub
   806	
   807	Before cleanup, present the synthesized plan + acceptance + `diff_lines` estimate via `AskUserQuestion` (**accept** / **regenerate** / **cancel**). On **accept**:
   808	
   809	1. Compose `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/composed-plan.md` containing `## Plan`, `## Acceptance`, and a trailing `diff_lines: <N>` line (integer from `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/diff-lines.txt` or best-effort estimate).
   810	2. Run `cat "$DESIGN_TMPDIR/composed-plan.md" | "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/redact-secrets.sh" > "$DESIGN_TMPDIR/composed-plan.redacted.md"`.
   811	3. Run `"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/plan-block-write.sh" --issue "$ISSUE_NUMBER" --content-file "$DESIGN_TMPDIR/composed-plan.redacted.md"`.
   812	4. Set `PLAN_WRITE_OK=true` on success; on failure print `**⚠ 5: plan-block-write failed — preserving $DESIGN_TMPDIR**`, set `PLAN_WRITE_OK=false`, and skip cleanup below.
   813	
   814	On **cancel**, exit **0** with `**ℹ /design cancelled by operator.**` after optional Step 5a bookkeeping.
   815	
   816	### 5c — Remove temp directory
   817	
   818	Remove the session temp directory and all files within it. Run `cleanup-tmpdir.sh` only when `PLAN_WRITE_OK=true` AND `STANDALONE_HEAVY_FAILED` is unset or `false`; otherwise skip cleanup so `$DESIGN_TMPDIR` is preserved for inspection.
   819	
   820	```bash
   821	if [ -z "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-}" ] && [ -n "${SESSION_ENV_PATH:-}" ] && [ -f "$SESSION_ENV_PATH" ]; then
   822	  CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT=$(awk 'BEGIN{p="LARCH_CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT="} index($0,p)==1{print substr($0,length(p)+1); exit}' "$SESSION_ENV_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true)
   823	fi
   824	export CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT
   825	${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.sh --dir "$DESIGN_TMPDIR"
   826	```
   827	
   828	**Plan helper contracts** (per `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/rules/script-md-siblings.md`):
   829	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/design-driver.sh` — ACTION dispatcher. Sibling: `design-driver.md`.
   830	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/classify-issue.sh` — classifier for legacy ACTION paths. Sibling: `classify-issue.md`.
   831	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/emit-plan.sh` — `ACTION=EMIT_PLAN`. Sibling: `emit-plan.md`.
   832	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/tally-plan-review.sh` — `ACTION=TALLY`. Sibling: `tally-plan-review.md`.
   833	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/finalize-plan.sh` — `ACTION=FINALIZE`. Sibling: `finalize-plan.md`.
   834	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/plan-block-write.sh` — writes the `larch:plan` block into the issue body. Sibling: `plan-block-write.md` (under `scripts/`).
   835	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/write-run-params.sh` — persists tier-derived `run-params.json` (Step 0). Sibling: `write-run-params.md`.
   836	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/write-design-manifest.md` — manifest writer contract (regression harness / Makefile targets only).
   837	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/read-design-manifest.md` — manifest reader contract (regression harness only).
   838	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/test-design-manifest.md` — regression harness contract for manifest reader/writer.
   839	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/write-design-manifest.sh` — manifest writer implementation (regression harness only).
   840	- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/design/scripts/read-design-manifest.sh` — manifest reader implementation (regression harness only).
   841	
   842	**Repeat any external reviewer warnings** from earlier steps (Step 0 reviewer-availability checks via `session-setup.sh`, Step 2a sketch-phase failures/timeouts, Step 3 runtime failures, or Step 3b diagram generation failure) so they are visible at the end of the workflow. For example:
   843	- `**⚠ Codex not available: <reason>**`
   844	- `**⚠ Cursor review failed: <reason>**`
   845	- `**⚠ Cursor sketch timed out / produced empty output**`
   846	- `**⚠ Codex sketch timed out / produced empty output**`
   847	- `**⚠ 3b: arch diagram — generation failed, proceeding without diagram (<elapsed>)**`
   848	
   849	Do NOT write any farewell message such as "Design complete", "Returning to the /implement orchestrator", "Handing back control", or any other prose that signals the skill is done — those are halts in disguise.
   850	
   851	When `PLAN_WRITE_OK=true`, emit exactly one terminal machine footer as the **last output line** of this skill (after repeating warnings, or immediately after cleanup when there are none). Do not emit anything after it:
   852	
   853	`➡️ 5: cleanup — plan written to issue #<N>; NEXT REQUIRED: continue`

