1. [correctness] `plan.txt:34-38,122`, `skills/design/SKILL.md:237-245`, `scripts/create-pr.sh:117-157`: the plan does not isolate the log PR from the current feature branch. Because `/design` may reuse an existing user branch and `create-pr.sh` intentionally returns an existing open PR for that branch, the proposed auto-merge can merge unrelated implementation commits. Use a dedicated logs-only branch or hard-refuse unless the PR head and diff are exclusively `larch-logs/design/<run-id>/`.

2. [security] `plan.txt:38,108-110`, `scripts/merge-pr.sh:11-15,139-157`: direct `gh pr merge --admin` bypasses the repo’s canonical admin-merge checks. If `[skip ci]` is required, put that exception behind an explicit logs-only path in `merge-pr.sh` with fresh-head and diff verification.

3. [security] `plan.txt:29-31,97-102`, `scripts/larch-log.md:18-24`, `SECURITY.md:130-136`: publishing all tempdir files with only generic redaction would commit sidecars that existing log publication deliberately trims. Add an allowlist and sidecar sanitizers before committing design logs.

4. [architecture] `plan.txt:27-28,108`, `scripts/larch-log.md:8-16`, `scripts/larch-log.sh:140-188`: the plan creates a second, partial manifest schema under `larch-logs/`. Reuse the existing manifest writer or define a separately versioned design-log schema instead of calling it schema version 2.
